{"id": "28053", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=28053", "title": "Pontiac (Illinois)", "text": "Pontiac is a small city of about 12000 people on old Route 66 in Central Illinois.\nGet in and around.\nMost visitors to Pontiac arrive by motorcar as part of a Route 66 tour, originating in Chicago and heading westward. The portion of US 66 which crosses Illinois from the windy city to St. Louis has been entirely bypassed by Interstate 55; either road leads to Pontiac."}
